Subject: [PATCH] BlitzInfer: route safetensors weights iterator through shared pool

Replace vLLM's `multi_thread_safetensors_weights_iterator` with the
BlitzInfer version (blitzinfer/loader/pinned_loader.py). When the env
vars BLITZ_SHARED_POOL + BLITZ_SHARDS_LAYOUT are set (the gateway sets
them per swap), the iterator reads weight tensors as views into the
parent's 80 GB hugetlbfs pool instead of `f.readinto`-ing safetensors
files from disk. Subprocess does cudaHostRegister on the same shared
file in its own CUDA context, then copies pool → GPU at PCIe wire
speed (~44-48 GB/s on PCIe 5.0).

If neither env var is set, the iterator falls back to the private-pool
path and behaves like vLLM's stock loader (so this is also a no-op
when running plain `vllm serve` outside the gateway).

Targets vLLM 0.20.1.

--- a/vllm/model_executor/model_loader/default_loader.py
+++ b/vllm/model_executor/model_loader/default_loader.py
@@ -34,6 +34,11 @@
     safetensors_weights_iterator,
 )

+# === BlitzInfer pinned-staged loader override ===
+from blitzinfer.loader.pinned_loader import (
+    multi_thread_safetensors_weights_iterator,  # noqa: F401, F811
+)
+
 from vllm.tracing import instrument
 from vllm.transformers_utils.repo_utils import list_filtered_repo_files
